# Security headers for the homepage, matching what Titan sets on its own
# responses. A static marketing page is a smaller target than an agent console,
# but these cost nothing and the two should not disagree about the basics.
#
# form-action is 'self' rather than 'none' because the access form posts to
# /api/access on this origin. It was 'none' while the page had no form at all,
# and left that way it blocks the submission in the BROWSER — no request is
# made, nothing is logged, and the page simply sits there. A missing endpoint
# and a blocked submission look identical from the outside, which is why the
# header and the endpoint have to move together.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'
